  "deliveredContent": "[hrc-runtime/turn-consolidation \u00b7 cody@hrc-runtime:T-08201 (gen 1) \u2192 you]\nHALT acknowledged. Current state: reproduction finished only; source tree untouched (`git status --short` is empty). No edit, commit, install, or restart occurred, and I will not re-dispatch the terminated smoke seat.\n\nFresh specimen on `agent:cody:project:hrc-runtime:task:T-08201:role:smoke` / `rt-e8f93ecc`:\n- original run `run-6d4a341b-ed5e-4e8c-91fe-6799e6d7df04`: `turn.started` at hrc_seq 1831414;\n- steer run `run-9e9c26c5-8b2c-484c-be29-0410ca4a1d92`: `turn.accepted` at 1831500, with broker diagnostics door/admissionClass `steer`, handed to harness, no turn start;\n- semantic `turn.completed` at 1831765 was attributed to the steer run, not the original. Because you terminated the specimen, the raw broker terminal was `turn.interrupted`; this confirms the shared interrupted terminal path has the same theft. The original `hrc turn --stacked 20s --stall-after 2m` observer exited 1 on stall while filtered on run-6d4a.\nI recorded the full discriminator in T-08201 comment C-19850.\n\nRead-only trace: `turn-dispatch-handlers.ts:418` mints a fresh run for every door; the headless/interactive broker handlers insert it as accepted and bind the returned submission id. `event-mapper.ts:753-755` prefers disposition-turn lookup; `findRunByDispositionTurnId` at 1037-1050 maps `submission.absorbed(turnId=<active turn>)` to the steer submission's run. The shared completed/failed/interrupted projection then terminalizes/emits against that resolved steer run.\n\nAdmission spec: `hrc-runtime.harness-broker-admission-client` explicitly says steer has no wait, obligation, or own-response option and resolves only via truthful `absorbed` or `executed`. That agrees with active-turn `absorbed`; I found no conflict. It does not dictate whether HRC omits the auxiliary run or marks it coalesced.",
